lantern-pr 1
# 42
#title Quit on the last window close without a reachable tray
#url https://github.com/MobileReality/lantern/pull/42
#branch feat/quit-on-last-window-without-tray
#base main
#opened 2026-11-12
#head 453ccf6b9601105ae060ac94b914b840194b1adb
#describe what Closing the last window quits Lantern on Windows and Linux unless a reachable tray icon exists; macOS is unchanged.
#describe what It quits through the normal quit path and never while a quit is already running.
#describe before The window-all-closed handler did nothing, so closing the last window on stock GNOME left an invisible process.
#describe after Linux without a tray host quits, KDE and similar desktops with a tray stay, Windows stays only with a tray, macOS never quits.
#describe verified Typecheck, lint and tests pass; the new tests fail when the macOS or Linux rule is removed. Not run on a real Linux or Windows machine.
+ src/main/last-window.ts
+ test/last-window.test.ts
~ src/main/main.ts
~ src/main/windows.ts
~ test/windows.test.ts
#order src/main/last-window.ts
#order src/main/windows.ts
#order src/main/main.ts
#order test/last-window.test.ts
#order test/windows.test.ts
#reason src/main/last-window.ts Keeps the quit decision a pure function so each platform and tray case can be tested without Electron
#reason test/last-window.test.ts Pins every platform and tray state, the Linux desktop list and the no-double-quit guard with a fake quit
#reason src/main/main.ts An empty window-all-closed handler left an invisible Lantern running on GNOME, so it now quits via the normal path
#reason src/main/windows.ts A hidden notification window stops window-all-closed from firing, so the last user window closing reports idle itself
#reason test/windows.test.ts Proves the idle callback fires only once the last window has closed
#story Closing the last window on Windows and Linux
#step actor A user on Linux or Windows
#file src/main/windows.ts
#step action closes the last Lantern window
#file src/main/main.ts
#step subject Lantern, which checks for a tray the user can reach
#file src/main/last-window.ts
#file test/last-window.test.ts
#below interaction Quit with the window, or stay in the tray where one can be clicked
#file test/windows.test.ts
#below consequence Lantern kept running with nothing to click on GNOME => Lantern quits cleanly unless a reachable tray exists
